Cell["\<\
On the square and the triangular tilings the deviation falls at the same \
threshold to a floor, the staircase of a segment off the lattice directions.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9860791a-e169-4e63-af40-04e903507e37"],

Cell["\<\
The deviation is blind to a closed loop: a member that circles a face stays \
close to its short chord. On the hexagonal tiling it does not see the \
threshold at all, since a straight extension zigzags as far from its chord as \
a bent one.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4d8c3fc1-c0a7-4a9d-90c6-c34f886a023f"],

Cell["The spread of the endpoints against the scale.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cdba69f8-a166-45b7-b5ec-97bf3ce0d4d5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

